# S-044 quirk Q: the mix buffers are float, but the region that is copied/clamped is 1024 * block_size bytes, where
# block_size depends on the *output format*. For FLOAT_PLANAR it is 1024 floats per plane; for 16-bit planar only 512
# floats per plane are clamped (the rest stays unclamped); for interleaved float stereo one plane of 2048 floats.
afeed_clear
aopen main 48000 16BIT_PLANAR STEREO
aconnect a 1 0
afeed 0 0 0 1024 3 set
aprobe 0 511 512 1023
atick
aclose
aopen main 48000 FLOAT STEREO
aconnect a 1 0
afeed_clear
afeed 0 0 0 2100 3 set
aprobe 0 1023 1024 2047 2048
atick
ainfo
aclose
aopen main 48000 U8BIT_PLANAR STEREO
aconnect a 1 0
afeed_clear
afeed 0 0 0 1024 3 set
aprobe 0 255 256 1023
atick
aclose
